WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.530
At five days old, a human embryo is a
hollow ball of about 100 to 200 cells.

2
00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:11.300
In an IVF clinic, embryos at this stage
are usually transferred to the womb, or

3
00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:12.520
frozen.

4
00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:16.310
Scientists can test embryos for
serious inherited conditions,

5
00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:18.520
and can even change genes.

6
00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:23.000
So is a five-day-old embryo
a person, a future person,

7
00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:25.210
or just a cluster of cells?

8
00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:29.460
In this mission, you'll follow an
embryo's first days on a timeline.

9
00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:33.280
Then you'll hear why some call
changing embryos playing God,

10
00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:36.290
while others call it
using God-given skill.

11
00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:40.590
Your mission: weigh up the different
views on the status of an early embryo.
